    "construction": {
      "outcome": "Repair only current owned-prefix reader premise in the existing native semantic revision component harness, preserving all meaningful assertions and historical limits.",
      "instructions": [
        "# N9-RETAINED-FIXTURE-01 only\n\nProduct Frame: ABIogenesis5 fixed fifteen families / GOAL-035 / T-287 / exact STDO3.0.4 manifest102817a3f4bea4dca1d6fa0fc634b94404dd2ba82ba6d8c38b273402dda9f95b / empty composition. Source e7179b19 on codex/t287-5-release-qualification; immutable installed RC6 remains unchanged. This is a component-proof prerequisite repair, not whole D2 or release qualification.\n\nApply exact installed stdo-work with its relative references. Repair only the local admitted-prefix premise in t287-native-semantic-revision.test.mjs: current semantic_revision.nativeIntakeFacts consumes event_prefix.readOwnedRuntimeEventPrefixAtDurablePrefix, while this harness still overrides Event Store's old reader and accidentally attempts file:///component/no-journal. Supply the supported current lower-owner premise through the existing component mechanism. The harness is explicitly synthetic/lookup-only; do not pretend to admit a store/prefix, add a new interface, or alter production to accommodate it.\n\nPreserve the existing first test's real owner logic and assertions: absent/ambiguous cause refusals, ancestry mismatch, unique eligible parent/cause, unrelated Run behavior, judgment/event ordering, serialized selection/request, publication/binding/currentness and remaining correction/evidence assertions. Do not stop at a port-spy assertion or change expected native_revision_cause_absent into the incidental exception. Keep all seven existing tests; the two captured-envelope historical gates remain honest exclusions. Do not add a skip, lower a floor, activate old archives or weaken errors.\n\nNative write grant is only this test file plus standard qualification-scratch/fixture-01 handoffs/tmp. The current premise is local; no support, production or HOW write is granted. A real Product counterexample or further write dependency returns to Root. No further functionality.\n\nFor mechanical author proof and C2, use the exact immutable RC6 build/contracts/dependencies staged into an isolated test sandbox and the selected source test/support files. The main ABI5_GENERIC_JOB_BUILD_ROOT override alone is insufficient: forward-command-harness also has literal ../../build/code/src imports. Copy only the existing immutable executable/dependency subtrees into the sandbox's standard build/contracts/node_modules locations; never overwrite repaired test sources. No tsc/generation/pack/npm-install is required for this test-only change.\n\nRun the existing full seven-test module using Node --experimental-vm-modules --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-reporter=tap. Expected current closure:5pass/0fail/2explicit historical skips. Existing first-test assertions must actually execute. Record exact actual results, including any newly reached failure; no fabricated green. No native actor/command/journal runs inside this component proof are claimed. Keep ABI5_EVIDENCE_ROOT unset for this bounded ungated component lane, preserving original historical input absence and limits.\n\nOne xhigh native coding Worker owns this increment. Return return/readiness/progress with exact hashes, changed premise and justified lower-owner assumptions, meaningful existing assertion evidence and all failures/skips. Freeze and stop. Root conjoins independent review, actual Testing/UAT and fresh closure. No Product release/qualification completion or reserved human acceptance.\n",
        "Root ROOT_CONTROL_SELECTION.json adopts the finite grant, including /private/tmp/abg-r6f1 temporary effects. METHOD_ACCESS.json binds exact installed STDO3.0.4 direct-file skill access and its relative references; no local .claude skill copy is required. Native provider scratch is tmpqf01, separate from test scratch. Preserve compiled checkout/build and all other files. For author selfcheck, use qualification-scratch/fixture-01/tmp as an isolated staging root with the ten selected test/support files and package.json at the same relative tenant paths, then clone the exact installed RC6 build/contracts/node_modules into that isolated tenant and run the selected Node test flags. Do not run the fixed C2 wrapper twice in one output directory. Tools are general host capabilities; exclusions are behavioral. Return missing prerequisites to Root without broadening."
      ],
